Subject: [PATCH] mmc: bcm2835_sdhost: forget a failed command

bcm2835_finish_command() and bcm2835_transmit() return early on an error and
leave host->cmd (and host->data, host->use_busy) set. The next command then
trips WARN_ON(host->cmd) in bcm2835_send_command(). On a Raspberry Pi 3 without
an SD card every probe of the slot times out, so the console fills with
"WARNING at drivers/mmc/bcm2835_sdhost.c:414" lines.

Clear the request state when bcm2835_send_cmd() fails, as Linux does in
bcm2835_finish_request().
---
diff --git a/drivers/mmc/bcm2835_sdhost.c b/drivers/mmc/bcm2835_sdhost.c
index 72012746..8fa9fc86 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/bcm2835_sdhost.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/bcm2835_sdhost.c
@@ -708,6 +708,17 @@ static int bcm2835_send_cmd(struct udevice *dev, struct mmc_cmd *cmd,
 			break;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * A failed request is over: forget it, as Linux does in
+	 * bcm2835_finish_request(). Otherwise the next command finds host->cmd
+	 * still set and WARN_ON() fires, e.g. on every probe of an empty slot.
+	 */
+	if (ret) {
+		host->cmd = NULL;
+		host->data = NULL;
+		host->use_busy = false;
+	}
+
 	return ret;
 }
 
